.TH SWAP 3
.SH NAME
swap \- integral representation conversion routines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft CR
#include <swap.h>
.sp
ssize_t swapop(const void* \fIinternal\fP, const void* \fIexternal\fP, ssize_t \fIwidth\fP);
.br
intmax_t swapget(int \fIop\fP, const void* \fIfrom\fP, size_t \fIwidth \fP);
.br
void* swapput(int \fIop\fP, void* \fIto\fP, size_t \fIwidth\fP, intmax_t \fIvalue\fP);
.br
void* swapmem(int \fIop\fP, const void* \fIfrom\fP, void* \fIto\fP, size_t \fIn\fP);
.ft
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These routines convert integral constants between internal and
external representations.
They are used to handle binary data generated by foreign programs.
New binary data representations should use the compact canonical form
provided by the
.IR sfio (3)
routines
\f[CB]sfputu\fP
and
\f[CB]sgetu\fR.
.PP
\f[CB]swapop\fP
returns the swap operation required to convert the
.I width
byte integer
.I external
to the
.I width
byte integer
.IR internal .
The swap operation is a bit mask:
.TP
\f[CB]0\fP
No swapping necessary.
.TP
\f[CB]1\fP
Swap byte
\f[CB]0\fP
with byte
\f[CB]1\fR.
.TP
\f[CB]2\fP
Swap bytes
\f[CB]0\fP
and
\f[CB]1\fP
with bytes
\f[CB]2\fP
and
\f[CB]3\fR.
.TP
\f[CB]4\fP
Swap bytes
\f[CB]0-3\fP
with bytes
\f[CB]4-7\fR,
and so on.
The largest native integral type is defined by the type
\f[CB]intmax_t\fP
from the header
\f[CB]<ast.h>\fR.
.PP
\f[CB]swapget\fP
returns the
.I width
byte integer in the buffer
.IR from ,
swapped according to
.IR op .
.PP
\f[CB]swapput\fP
copies the
.I width
byte integer
.I value
into the buffer
.IR to ,
swapped according to
.IR op .
.I to
is returned.
.PP
\f[CB]swapmem\fP
swaps
\f[CB]n\fP
bytes from the buffer
.I from
to the buffer
.I to
according to
.IR op .
.I to
and
.I from
may be the same.
